      "setup": "A 32 by 41 m area (about 35 by 45 yards) in front of a goal with a goalkeeper, split lengthways into three zones, with two mini goals on the far line. Two centre backs stay in the middle zone and a fullback in each outside zone; four attackers move freely. Spare attackers and defenders wait to rotate in.",
      "instructions": [
        "An attacker starts with the ball at the far end; the four attackers have 10 seconds to combine and get a shot away.",
        "Defenders stay in their zones. If they win the ball they break out and score in either mini goal.",
        "The defending four switch after every two completed attacks, the attackers after every three."
      ],
      "coaching_points": [
        "Quick combinations to get in behind: one and two touches.",
        "A sharp movement creates the yard of space to finish.",
        "Exploit the fullbacks being stuck in their zones: attack the gaps beside them.",
        "Weight the penetrating pass and time the run in behind together.",
        "Defenders: move as a unit and keep talking."
      ],
